# Holidays and Work Schedule Policy
**Daisy Health**
**Policy ID:** HR-HS-008
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2025
**Last Reviewed:** June 1, 2025
**Owner:** People Operations

---

## Purpose

This policy outlines Daisy Health's observed holidays, work schedule expectations, and special scheduling considerations for clinical staff who support patients year-round.

---

## Scope

This policy applies to all full-time and part-time Daisy Health employees. Clinical staff should refer to Section 5 for additional scheduling guidance specific to patient care operations.

---

## 1. Company-Observed Holidays

Daisy Health observes the following paid holidays each year. All non-clinical employees have these days off with full pay.

| Holiday | 2025 Date |
|---|---|
| New Year's Day | January 1 (Wednesday) |
| Martin Luther King Jr. Day | January 20 (Monday) |
| Presidents' Day | February 17 (Monday) |
| Memorial Day | May 26 (Monday) |
| Juneteenth | June 19 (Thursday) |
| Independence Day | July 4 (Friday) |
| Labor Day | September 1 (Monday) |
| Indigenous Peoples' Day | October 13 (Monday) |
| Veterans Day | November 11 (Tuesday) |
| Thanksgiving Day | November 27 (Thursday) |
| Day After Thanksgiving | November 28 (Friday) |
| Christmas Day | December 25 (Thursday) |

When a holiday falls on a Saturday, it is observed on the preceding Friday. When it falls on a Sunday, it is observed on the following Monday.

---

## 2. Floating Holidays

In addition to company-observed holidays, all full-time employees receive **2 floating holidays** per calendar year. Floating holidays:

- May be used on any day of the employee's choosing
- Must be scheduled with at least **3 business days notice** to your manager
- Do not roll over to the next year — unused floating holidays expire on December 31
- Are prorated for employees hired after July 1 (1 floating holiday for the remainder of the year)

Part-time employees receive 1 floating holiday per year.

---

## 3. Standard Work Hours

Daisy Health operates on a flexible, remote-first schedule. However, employees are expected to maintain consistent working hours that overlap with their team and support their responsibilities.

### Core Hours

All employees are expected to be available and responsive during **core hours of 10 AM – 3 PM in their local time zone**, Monday through Friday, unless otherwise agreed with their manager.

### Flexible Hours

Outside of core hours, employees have flexibility in how they structure their workday, provided they:

- Meet all job responsibilities and deadlines
- Attend scheduled meetings and clinical shifts
- Communicate schedule changes to their manager in advance

### Full-Time Hours

Full-time employees are expected to work approximately **40 hours per week**. Exempt (salaried) employees are not paid overtime but should speak with their manager if workload consistently exceeds 40 hours per week.

---

## 4. Part-Time Schedules

Part-time employees work between 20–29 hours per week as defined in their offer letter. Specific schedules are set by the employee and their manager. Changes to a part-time schedule require manager approval and must be updated in the HR system.

---

## 5. Clinical Staff Scheduling

Daisy Health provides virtual primary care to patients across multiple time zones. Clinical operations run **7 days a week, 7 AM – 10 PM ET**. Clinical staff have scheduling requirements that differ from non-clinical employees.

### Shift-Based Scheduling

Clinical employees (physicians, NPs, PAs, RNs, clinical pharmacists, behavioral health counselors) are scheduled in shifts. Shifts are assigned by the Clinical Operations team in coordination with your clinical manager.

Standard shift options include:

- Morning: 7 AM – 3 PM ET
- Midday: 11 AM – 7 PM ET
- Evening: 2 PM – 10 PM ET

Shift schedules are published **4 weeks in advance**. Requests to change shifts must be submitted at least **2 weeks before** the affected date.

### Holiday Coverage for Clinical Staff

Because patients need care every day, clinical staff rotate holiday coverage. Each clinical employee is expected to work **at least 2 company-observed holidays per year**.

Clinical staff who work on a company-observed holiday receive:

- Their regular pay for the shift, plus
- **Holiday premium pay of 1.5x** for hours worked on the holiday, plus
- One additional **floating holiday** to use within 90 days

Holiday shift assignments are made by the Clinical Operations team and communicated at least 30 days in advance. Employees who cannot work an assigned holiday shift must find a swap with a qualified colleague and notify their manager.

### On-Call Requirements

Some clinical roles require on-call availability outside of scheduled shifts. On-call requirements are specified in your role description and offer letter. On-call employees must:

- Be reachable by phone or secure message within 15 minutes
- Be able to begin a clinical encounter within 30 minutes if needed
- Not consume alcohol or substances that would impair clinical judgment during on-call hours

On-call compensation is outlined in your offer letter and the Compensation Policy (HR-PC-011).

---

## 6. Schedule Changes and Swaps

Employees who need to change their work schedule temporarily should:

1. Request the change with at least **3 business days notice** to their manager
2. For clinical shift swaps, identify a qualified colleague willing to swap and confirm with the Clinical Operations team
3. Document the change in the scheduling system

Repeated last-minute schedule changes without notice may result in a formal discussion with your manager.

---

## 7. Inclement Weather and Emergency Closures

Because Daisy Health is a remote-first company, inclement weather closures generally do not apply. However, in the event of a declared local emergency or natural disaster affecting an employee's ability to work:

- Notify your manager as soon as possible
- Clinical staff must notify the Clinical Operations team immediately so coverage can be arranged
- People Operations will communicate any company-wide guidance via email and Slack

